; The core links the one instrumentation runtime (lib/runtime): the
; coverage seam snapshots its registry, the mutation loop drives its
; catalogue and writes verdicts through its file format, and both spell
; identifiers with the runtime's own functions so the report and the
; runtime cannot disagree. The dependency points downward only — the
; runtime never links windtrap.

(library
 (name windtrap)
 (public_name windtrap)
 (libraries unix windtrap_runtime)
 ; Windtrap measures its own coverage. The backend is spelled
 ; `ppx_windtrap.coverage`, not the `ppx_windtrap` the manual shows
 ; users: that name resolves to the inline-test rewriter, whose
 ; ppx_runtime_libraries would put ppx_windtrap.runtime — and through it
 ; this very library — into its own closure, which is a dependency cycle.
 ; See ppx/coverage/dune. Inert without --instrument-with: a plain
 ; `dune runtest` builds and runs exactly as before.
 (instrumentation
  (backend ppx_windtrap.coverage))
 ; And windtrap mutates itself. Five modules opt out with
 ; [@@@mutate exclude_file] — the scheduler, the ambient run state, the
 ; reporting spine, the mutation loop and the facade — because a mutant
 ; there is armed inside the process that is supposed to judge it, and
 ; the failure mode is a hang rather than a survivor. The inline
 ; runtime, excluded for the same reason, lives above the core
 ; (ppx/runtime) in a library whose dune carries no mutation stanza at
 ; all. The tree's own mutation suites scope their runs to their fixture
 ; directories (see doc/dev/testing.md), so an instrumented core adds
 ; nothing to the population they fork over.
 (instrumentation
  (backend ppx_windtrap.mutate))
 (foreign_stubs
  (language c)
  (names capture_stubs clock_stubs env_stubs)))
